# PERF-BESTSPLIT-RIDER A/B — 2026-06-10
#
# Change: BestSplit side-costs rider (issue #64 follow-on, deferred from
# PERF-HIST-SUB-LOSSLESS). `find_best_split` / `find_best_split_borrowed`
# already compute each threshold's left/right entropy cost during the
# sweep; `BestSplit` now carries the winning threshold's `left_bits` /
# `right_bits` out, and all six engine call sites consume them instead of
# re-running `compute_predictor_entropy` twice per split (2 x O(n_side)):
#   compute_best_tree (parallel root + sequential loop),
#   build_subtree_sequential, build_subtree_recursive_parallel,
#   build_subtree_{sequential,recursive_parallel}_borrowed,
#   compute_best_tree_with_multipliers (split-predictor site only — its
#   second site re-derives predictors independently and keeps the
#   recompute; the test-side reference_greedy_tree_no_tensors also keeps
#   the naive recompute deliberately, as an independent verifier).
#
# ── Bitwise-identity argument + proof ───────────────────────────────────────
# Sweep and recompute both call jxl_simd::estimate_bits_u32 over a
# `..histogram_size` slice (`effective_histo == histogram_size` in BOTH
# split fns — the "max token narrowing" doc bullet was stale), on u32
# histograms accumulated from the same weighted sample multiset (integer,
# order-free) plus the same u64 `eb * count` sums. Identical inputs to the
# same deterministic dispatch => identical f64.
# Enforced permanently: `debug_verify_carried_side_bits{,_borrowed}` re-runs
# the recompute and asserts bitwise equality at every consuming site in
# debug builds (test/dev profiles keep debug-assertions on; release strips
# the verify entirely via cfg!).
# Proof runs (all on the rider tree):
#   - cargo test -p jxl-encoder: 1870 passed (asserts silent on every split
#     of every encode). 1 pre-existing parallel-suite env flake, see
#     CLAUDE.md Known Bugs 2026-06-10 (passes in isolation; 9 it-files
#     mutate process env).
#   - hash_lock_features 36/36 default AND 36/36 --features
#     parallel-tree-learning.
#   - strategy_libjxl_byte_lock 5/5 (--features __expert).
#   - Debug ptl encodes of clic097 + terminal at --lossless e7: asserts
#     silent (borrowed engines on real content).
#   - just rd-regression: RED on the first run for a PRE-EXISTING
#     environment reason — ADDENDUM (same day): root cause was the 5
#     CID22-512 images, which codec-corpus auto-DOWNLOADED during that
#     first failing run; the re-run is GREEN 2/2 with frymire's favorable
#     post-2c drift inside tolerances. No baseline change was needed and
#     none was made. (The meta's original "clic2025/validation missing"
#     attribution was wrong for rd-regression — that dir was renamed to
#     clic2025/training and only ignored/visual tests referenced it;
#     refs re-pointed same day.) Not caused by this change either way.
#
# ── A/B grid (this file's .tsv) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Binaries: BASE from git 98c5c713 (exported via git archive to a sibling
# dir), OURS from the rider tree. BOTH sides built from $HOME with
# --manifest-path + --locked --offline against the SAME Cargo.lock (the
# repo's untracked on-disk lock, copied to the sibling), bypassing the
# temporary ~/work/zen/.cargo/config.toml paths-override on BOTH sides —
# identical dep sources and versions. default-features binaries for 1T
# cells; +parallel-tree-learning for the 8T cell. 6 iters/side,
# interleaved b,o,b,o..., 1 warmup/side, median reported
# (scripts/bench_lossless_ab.py).
#
# BYTES: identical base-vs-ours on ALL 7 lossless cells (sha256, every
# iteration, both sides also self-deterministic). Lossy probes byte-
# identical too: frymire e5 d=1.0 and clic097 e7 d=1.0 (the clic probe was
# re-run with the correct filename after the in-grid one hit a wrong-path
# bug and compared stale files — the in-grid "LOSSY-IDENTICAL clic097"
# line in the run log is void; the re-run stands).
#
# WALL: NOT RESOLVABLE in this grid — the box ran other agents' un-niced
# jobs throughout (rustc 434%, zenpng 226%, then zenjxl_decoder ~2300%;
# loadavg 5.3 -> 19.9 over the run). Interleaving keeps the deltas
# unbiased but the spread (-1.90% .. +3.26%, control cell terminal at
# -0.05%) is noise-dominated. The change strictly REMOVES release-build
# work (two O(n_side) passes per split; adds 16 bytes to one per-node
# struct and two f64 stores per best-threshold update), so a real
# regression is not structurally plausible; queue a quiet-machine wall
# re-run (same script, same cells) next time loadavg < 2 before citing
# any wall number from this rider.
#
# ── ADDENDUM (same day): QUIET-MACHINE RE-RUN — wall resolved ──────────────
# Same script, same cells, same binaries; loadavg 0.74 at start, 2.28 at
# end (perf_bestsplit_rider_2026-06-10.quiet.tsv):
#   clic097_e7  1T  -1.84%   clic097_e9 1T  -1.48%   clic028_e7 1T -1.34%
#   clic097_e7  8T  -0.80%   (photos = the split-bound class)
#   terminal_e7 1T  +1.27%   mobile_substack +0.57%  noaa_leslie -0.07%
#   (controls — not split-bound; within run-to-run noise on sub-second /
#   document cells. The noisy grid's noaa +3.26% collapsed to -0.07%,
#   confirming it was load noise.)
# Verdict: small consistent wall win exactly where the removed work
# lives — lossless photos -1.3..-1.8% at 1T (e7 AND e9), -0.8% at 8T —
# and no effect elsewhere. Bytes identical 7/7 again on the quiet grid.
#
# Cells: clic097/clic028 (CLIC-1024 photos, e7+e9 1T; photos are the
# split-bound class), terminal (gb82-sc screenshot control — not
# split-bound, expected ~0), noaa_leslie 8.4MP doc + mobile_substack
# 2.7MP (lossless_bench_set_2026-06-10 core picks), clic097 e7 8T (ptl,
# borrowed engines).
#
# Host: lilith (7950X, 128 GB, WSL2). No -C target-cpu=native.
# Reproduce: scripts/bench_lossless_ab.py --base <base-bin> --ours
# <ours-bin> --iters 6 --out <tsv> --cell name:glob:effort:threads ...
